  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Improving Social Protection and Health 2</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">ISPH 2 will be Australia&#x2019;s flagship investment in social protection to reduce inequality and improve development and economic outcomes for Cambodia&#x2019;s most marginalised groups. ISPH 2 is a partner-led design that is implemented and co-financed by Germany&#x2019;s Deutsche Gesellschaft f&#xfc;r Internationale Zusammenarbeit (GIZ). Its goal is to work alongside the Cambodian Government and support their efforts to effectively implement its social protection policy agenda and improve the systems and structures that tie all efforts together, underpinned by sufficient and sustainable government financing. This goal is supported by one End of Investment Outcome (EOIO) and four Intermediate Outcomes (IO), with DFAT contributing to IOs 1,2 and 3. IPSH 2&apos;s EOIO is: The prerequisites for better access to social protection and quality-assured health services in Cambodia have improved with regard to responsiveness to climate related risks, gender-responsiveness, inclusiveness and poverty reduction.</narrative>
  </description>
